<%# The Cornell University Library lockup, per the Library branding guide:
    the red lockup on light backgrounds, the white lockup on dark ones. These
    pages follow the reader's system color scheme (see mcp.scss), so the swap
    is done the same way, with a media query rather than a class. The seal is
    120px tall on a desktop, the guide's digital minimum, and scales down on
    a phone. %>
<a class="mcp-brand d-inline-block mb-4" href="https://www.library.cornell.edu/">
  <picture>
    <source srcset="/img/CULibraryWhite.svg" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
    <img class="mcp-lockup" src="/img/CULibraryRed.svg" alt="Cornell University Library" width="382" height="120">
  </picture>
</a>
